{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-anima/1500950-default-numbers-of-tags-in-anima-era","id":1500950,"title":"Default Numbers of Tags in Anima Era","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Anima"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-21T11:19:34-08:00","id":1500950,"title":"Default Numbers of Tags in Anima Era","content":"I was curious how many tags you all plan to give equipment in the Anima era. As I recall this is not covered in the manuscript, but I admit I haven't read it since it came out. I would propose putting things somewhere between Core and Aeon for obvious linear time reasons. I was thinking 2+ wealth for weapons, 2 (or 3) + wealth for armor, and leaving vehicles at just wealth. What do you all think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T12:56:31-08:00","id":1500957,"title":"","content":"My approach would be same as Aeon, but without access to the psi specific tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-21T21:04:59-08:00","id":1501003,"title":"","content":"That seems as reasonable a solution as any, but I think I want Anima to be at least a little less advanced than Aeon. I tend to think that tech isn't generally as advanced as in Aeon because by the 2080's the world is still in the rebuilding phase. But that's just my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T08:55:43-08:00","id":1501037,"title":"","content":"Tech, IIRC, stagnates for a while after the Aberrant War as people worry that anything too advanced is related to Novas, with a lot of the newer technology by Aeon being (noetic) biotech because it's pretty to easy to prove it's not quantum stuff.<br /> <br /> As Anima IIRC mainly relies on hardtech it's probably at about the same level as Aeon, with some areas potentially lagging behind. Although my first thought would be 'unless stated otherwise assume corebook rules are meant to hold', so for Tags I'd say anything between core and Aeon is appropriate until a dev says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-22T11:07:27-08:00","id":1501042,"title":"","content":"I would say the big leap from Aberrant tech to Aeon tech was during Aberrant War.<br /> <br /> Sure people were afraid of novatech, but the advances made by humanity during Nova era and Aberrant War were literally supernatural and much of what was common during Aeon era was established as viable &quot;normal&quot; tech not after Aberrant war but prior it. If you check the text about the urban exodus/dyaspora/schism (not sure the correct word used) you notice most of the hardtech available in aeon was available just after Aberrant War.<br /> <br /> Humans devloped after it, sure, but it was not the same kind of leap Novas could source. And the presence of Psions only created a real boom in biotech, not hard tech (maybe some advances in other areas, but not a real boom).<br /> <br /> To make it clear, I would say Anima has all tech in Aeon level except for biotech tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}